  "title": "Chapter 36: Mountains of India",
  "order": 37,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f595e52",
      "content": "Mountains are an important physical feature of India. They influence the country's climate, drainage system, vegetation and human activities. The major mountain systems of India include the Himalayan Mountains and the Peninsular Mountains. These mountains also play an important role in protecting India from cold winds, influencing monsoon rainfall, and serving as the source of many important rivers."
    },
